text.section:
Any local school board may establish and implement policies to provide for the open enrollment to any school of any student residing within the school division upon the request of a parent or guardian. In developing such policies, a local school board may include the following conditions and limitations:

An application process whereby a parent or guardian indicates a school preference for purposes of his child attending a school in the child's school division but outside of the attendance area in which the child resides;


A requirement that the parent or guardian provide transportation for the student attending a school other than his assigned school;


A requirement that a student may be disqualified from attending a school other than his assigned school if he has been subject to a specified disciplinary action;


A prohibition on the recruitment of a student from one school to another by a school division employee;


A limitation on participation in certain athletic activities for a student who chooses to attend a school other than his assigned school;


A random, unbiased selection process in the event open enrollment requests exceed the capacity of a school;


A provision that a student shall be permitted to remain at the receiving school until the student has completed the highest grade level in the school; and


A preference to a student (i) who resides in a location that has been subject to a change in school attendance area during the previous two years, (ii) who has a sibling attending the receiving school, or (iii) whose parent or guardian is an employee of the receiving school.
